{"base_rate":0.28291316526610644,"brier":0.14853851540616247,"bss":0.26782622021967817,"bss_hi":0.3745346891595956,"bss_lo":0.16286183031548612,"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09799719887955184,"ess":519.914982671735,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for New York City</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The New York City rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>74%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 714 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nJERSEY CITY 1.6 NNE, 4.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 76 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(40&ndash;96) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>205</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>58%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>New York City</b> <span class=\"muted\">US</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>40&ndash;96\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>714 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    New York City &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for New York City\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 61.54,365.7014925373134 69.20253164556962,354.3544303797468 91.9368,323.76 145.07416666666666,255.61111111111111 252.94246575342467,142.65753424657535 358.5408695652174,44.37681159420288 410.37351351351356,18.0 410.37351351351356,27.83783783783781 358.5408695652174,102.40579710144931 252.94246575342467,217.57671232876712 145.07416666666666,326.3888888888889 91.9368,367.44 69.20253164556962,382.0 61.54,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"279.01960784313724\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"279.01960784313724\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,369.57073170731707 61.54,343.97014925373134 69.20253164556962,358.9620253164557 91.9368,318.90666666666664 145.07416666666666,230.33333333333331 252.94246575342467,172.57534246575344 358.5408695652174,155.15942028985506 410.37351351351356,111.45945945945948\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 205 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"369.57073170731707\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"61.54\" cy=\"343.97014925373134\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"69.20253164556962\" cy=\"358.9620253164557\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 10%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"91.9368\" cy=\"318.90666666666664\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"145.07416666666666\" cy=\"230.33333333333331\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 58% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"252.94246575342467\" cy=\"172.57534246575344\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"358.5408695652174\" cy=\"155.15942028985506\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.37351351351356\" cy=\"111.45945945945948\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(28%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In New York City the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.39) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.17).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.166</td><td class='num'>10.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>206</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.236</td><td class='num'>14.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.277</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>162</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>0.395</td><td class='num'>2.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":40.71427,"lon":-74.00597,"n":714,"n_cities":109,"name":"New York City","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":205,"obs":0.03414634146341464,"sig":true},{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.01,"n":67,"obs":0.1044776119402985,"sig":true},{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.03164556962025317,"n":79,"obs":0.06329113924050633,"sig":false},{"hi":0.15,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.09586666666666667,"n":75,"obs":0.17333333333333334,"sig":true},{"hi":0.37,"lo":0.15,"mean":0.24597222222222223,"n":72,"obs":0.4166666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":0.7039999999999997,"lo":0.37,"mean":0.5506849315068494,"n":73,"obs":0.5753424657534246,"sig":false},{"hi":0.97,"lo":0.7039999999999997,"mean":0.8489855072463768,"n":69,"obs":0.6231884057971014,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.97,"mean":0.9954054054054056,"n":74,"obs":0.7432432432432432,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.3,"rank":76,"rank_hi":96.0,"rank_lo":40.0,"reliability":0.016431016808965936,"resolution":0.07105260603488225,"slug":"new-york-city","station":"JERSEY CITY 1.6 NNE","timezone":"America/New_York"}